# Clerk Auth — Cursor Rules (thin pointer)

**Canonical auth guidance lives in [`.claude/rules/auth.md`](../../.claude/rules/auth.md).**

The guidance that previously lived in this file described a Clerk–Supabase
native integration that NO LONGER EXISTS — the app migrated to Neon PostgreSQL
with Drizzle ORM. Do not write Supabase JWT templates, `auth.jwt()` RLS
policies, or Supabase client wiring for auth. Session context flows through
`getSessionContext` (`apps/web/lib/auth/session`). Email-code auth is an
intentional, supported sign-in path alongside SSO.
